---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LONG_DISCLAIMER, REPORT_DISCLOSURE } from '@/lib/trustCopy';
const user = Astro.locals.user;
---
<BaseLayout user={user} seo={{ title: 'Terms of Service — CrossLinkd', description: 'Terms for using CrossLinkd, a community directory. Listing details are not independently verified, and inclusion is not an endorsement.', path: '/terms' }}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm" style="color:var(--text-mute)">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--text-soft)">
      <p>{LONG_DISCLAIMER}</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">1. A directory, not an endorsement.</strong> Listings may appear in search results, sorted lists, or highlighted areas. Placement and inclusion are not a theological endorsement, denominational approval, or independent assessment of a business.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">2. Accurate listings.</strong> Submitters are responsible for information they provide and must have the right to submit it. Any faith, ownership, license, or credential statement is supplied by the submitter; CrossLinkd does not independently verify listing details. Source labels are shown only when the source is recorded.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">3. Respectful conduct.</strong> Reviews and messages must follow our Community Guidelines and Review Policy. Harassment, hate, spam, impersonation, and misinformation are prohibited. {REPORT_DISCLOSURE} A report is not an automatic takedown.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">4. Regulated professions.</strong> Do not misstate licensure for counseling, healthcare, legal, financial, or contracting practices. CrossLinkd does not check license databases. Listing a license is not confirmation that it is current.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">5. Youth safety.</strong> If a listing serves minors, the submitter is responsible for complying with applicable law. CrossLinkd does not inspect safeguarding practices.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">6. Content you submit.</strong> You grant CrossLinkd a license to store, format, and display submitted content so the directory can operate. You keep ownership of that content. Deleting an account does not by itself unpublish a listing. Use the contact form to flag a correction or removal request; submitting a request does not guarantee an immediate change.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">7. Moderation.</strong> CrossLinkd may edit, suspend, or remove content that violates these terms. You can ask about a moderation decision through the <a href="/appeals" class="underline">appeals page</a>. Submitting an appeal does not guarantee a response or a changed decision.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">8. Limitation of liability.</strong> The service is provided “as is.” We are not liable for transactions or other dealings between users and listings. Read a profile and evaluate the organization for yourself.</p>
      <p><strong style="color:var(--text)">9. No fees right now.</strong> Listing and account forms do not ask for payment details. Basic listings, management requests, and accounts are free at this time. If a paid feature is introduced, its terms will be explained before billing begins. Payment would not create a verification or endorsement.</p>
      <p>Questions? <a href="/contact" class="underline">Contact us</a>. No response time is promised. See also: <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy</a>, <a href="/guidelines" class="underline">Guidelines</a>, <a href="/appeals" class="underline">Appeals</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
